The objective of eco-labels is to inform customers of the effects on the environment of the production, utilization and storage of the product, thereby changing the buying conduct and reductions in adverse effects in the end. Eco-labeling is seen as an efficient means for changing the behaviour of consumers purchasing. The cost and benefit of such environmental data must be measured to evaluate the financial effectiveness of identifying programmes for eco-labelling. In circularity, eco-labeling can increase trustability of the product through the inspection certification by the company or by a recognized institution.